</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM8"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM8_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 8: Figure S8. Upright stereotactic microinjection failed to reliably deliver chemicals into adult rat extrapontine trigeminal roots. (a) The stereotactic coordinates of extrapontine trigeminal roots in the MRI/DTI brain atlas of Wistar rats (250g) (MRI/DTI atlas of the rat Brain, 2015, Paxinos, G., Watson, C.). (b) Upright stereotactic microinjection into extrapontine trigeminal roots at the refined stereotactic coordinates could be either on target or off target in SD rats (250g). (c) The <italic>in situ</italic> morphology of extrapontine trigeminal roots in Wistar and SD rats based on MRI brain atlases (MRI/DTI atlas of the rat Brain, 2015, Paxinos, G., Watson, C., Waxholm Space atlas of the Sprague Dawley rat brain, 2014, Papp, E. A., Leergaard, T. B.). (d) The skulls of Wistar and SD rats. Reproduced and used with permissions from the authors as the copyright owners here (A study on head measurements in different laboratory rat strains, 2023, &#x000c7;al&#x00131;&#x0015f;&#x00131;r, M., &#x000dc;st&#x000fc;nda&#x0011f;, Y., doi:10.5505/TJHS.2023.09797). (e) Dorsal and medial view of extrapontine trigeminal roots in SD rats. (f) The partial and complete covering of extrapontine trigeminal roots by petrous ridges obstructs upright stereotactic microinjection in SD rats.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM9"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM9_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 9: Figure S9. <italic>In situ</italic>MRI anatomy supported the unreliability of upright stereotactic microinjection to target adult SD rat extrapontine trigeminal roots at the coronal plane of AP -7.20 mm (obstruction by the petrous ridge). N=3 animals. </p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM10"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM10_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 10: Figure S10. Temporal dynamics of trigeminal REZ demyelination in adult rats. Representative images of neutral red/FluoroMyelin staining. N = 3 animals per timepoint &#x000d7; treatment.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM11"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM11_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 11: Figure S11. The durations of asymmetric eyelid contraction (b) and the counts of asymmetric isolated/cluster face-stroking (c) evoked by von Frey filaments of increasing strength (a) in rat model of trigeminal REZ demyelination. N = 9 animals for LPC microinjection and N = 6 animals for PBS microinjection. Independent samples t-test for touch stimuli at each strength. <sup>**</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.01; <sup>***</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.001; <sup>****</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.0001. ns, no significance.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM12"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM12_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 12: Figure S12. The responsiveness of facial pain to carbamazepine versus pregabalin in rat chemical model of trigeminal REZ demyelination. Animals microinjected with LPC: N = 6 for vehicle, N = 7 for carbamazepine and N = 6 for pregabalin. 2W-RM ANOVA followed by &#x00160;&#x000ed;d&#x000e1;k's multiple comparisons test. After-drug versus before-drug: <sup>*</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.05; <sup>**</sup><italic> P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.01; <sup>***</sup><italic> P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.001; <sup>****</sup><italic> P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.0001.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM13"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM13_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 13: Figure S13. Schematic view of chemical silencer for primary nociceptive afferents (mainly TRPV1<sup>+</sup>). The charged, membrane-impermeable lidocaine derivative QX-314 is allowed to enter in primary nociceptive afferents through the pore of the TRPV1 channel that is opened by the co-applied TRPV1 agonist capsaicin, resulting in selective neuronal silencing. Created with bioRender.com.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM14"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM14_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 14: Figure S14. The requirement of primary nociceptive afferents for facial pain in rat chemical model of trigeminal REZ demyelination. N = 6 animals microinjected with LPC for either vehicle or chemical silencer. 2W-RM ANOVA followed by &#x00160;&#x000ed;d&#x000e1;k's multiple comparisons test. Post-silencing versus pre-silencing: <sup>*</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.05; <sup>**</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.01; <sup>****</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.0001.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM15"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM15_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 15: Figure S15.The efficiency and specificity of ~1.9 kb mouse MBP gene promoter in AAV2/9 serotype to drive the expression of exogenous genes with EGFP as an example after stereotactic microinjection into adult mice trigeminal REZs. (a) EGFP expression intensities in trigeminal REZs after stereotactic microinjection of AAV2/9:MBP(~1.9 kb)-EGFP in comparison with AAV2/9:MBP(~1.3 kb)-EGFP (~5E+12 vg/ml, 0.1 &#x003bc;l). (b) Oligodendroglial EGFP expression in trigeminal REZs after stereotactic microinjection of AAV2/9:MBP(~1.9 kb)-EGFP. (c) Neuronal EGFP expression in nearby trigeminal nuclei after stereotactic microinjection of AAV2/9:MBP(~1.9 kb)-EGFP. N = 3 animals per group or experiment.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM16"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM16_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 16: Figure S16. The rAAV-based conditional genetic tool that ablates neurons in nearby trigeminal nuclei via apoptosis. The changes of EGFP-labeled neurons after stereotactic microinjection into adult mice trigeminal REZs either AAV2/9:hSyn-Cre-EGFP + AAV2/9:CMV-DIO-taCasp3-TEVp mixture or AAV2/9:hSyn-Cre-EGFP (for each virus: ~5E+12 vg/ml, 0.1 &#x003bc;l). N = 4 animals per group. Independent samples t-test. <sup>**</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.05; <sup>**</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.01.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM17"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM17_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 17: Figure S17. The duration of asymmetric eyelid contraction and the counts of asymmetric isolated/cluster face-stroking evoked by von Frey hairs of increasing strength in viral genetic mouse model of trigeminal REZ demyelination. N = 7 animals for AAV2/9:MBP-Cre-EGFP + AAV2/9:CMV-DIO-taCasp3-TEVp mixture or AAV2/9:hSyn-Cre-EGFP + AAV2/9:CMV-DIO-taCasp3-TEVp mixture; N = 6 animals for AAV2/9:MBP-Cre-EGFP or AAV2/9-hSyn-Cre-eGFP. One way analysis of variance (ANOVA) followed by Tukey's multiple comparisons test for touch stimuli at each strength. <sup>*</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.05; <sup>**</sup><italic> P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.01; <sup>***</sup><italic> P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.001; <sup>****</sup><italic> P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.0001.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM18"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM18_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 18: Figure S18. The TN relevance of facial pain (asymmetric eyelid contraction here) evoked by von Frey hairs of increasing strength in viral genetic mouse model of trigeminal REZ demyelination. (a) The responsiveness of facial pain to carbamazepine versus pregabalin. Animals microinjected with AAV2/9:MBP(~1.3kb)-Cre-EGFP+ AAV2/9:CMV-DIO-taCasp3-TEVp mixture: N = 6 for either vehicle or carbamazepine or pregabalin. 2W-RM ANOVA followed by &#x00160;&#x000ed;d&#x000e1;k's multiple comparisons test. After-drug versus before-drug: <sup>*</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.05; <sup>**</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.01; <sup>****</sup><italic> P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.0001. (b) The requirement of primary nociceptive afferents. Animals microinjected with AAV2/9:MBP(~1.3kb)-Cre-EGFP+ AAV2/9:CMV-DIO-taCasp3-TEVp mixture: N = 6 animals for vehicle, N = 8 animals for chemical silencer. 2W-RM ANOVA followed by &#x00160;&#x000ed;d&#x000e1;k's multiple comparisons test. Post-silencing versus pre-silencing: <sup>*</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.05; <sup>****</sup><italic>P</italic>&#x0ff1c;0.0001.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM19"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM19_ESM.jpg"><caption><p>Additional file 19: Figure S19. <italic>In situ</italic> MRI anatomy informed coronal angled stereotactic microinjection into intrapontine trigeminal roots of adult SD rats. (a) The validation of the stereotactic coordinates for intrapontine trigeminal roots of adult SD rats via upright stereotactic microinjection along the ML axis (AP -9.86 mm, ML 2.75/2.85/2.95/3.05/3.25 mm, DV -8.50 mm) based on the MRI/DTI brain atlas of Wistar rats (MRI/DTI atlas of the rat Brain, 2015, Paxinos, G., Watson, C.). N = 3 animals per position. However, the upright stereotactic microinjection method was found to be error-prone during our pilot studies. The essential reason for this technical instability is that the intrapontine trigeminal roots are laterally curved, tilted anticlockwise, very narrow along the ML direction (~0.5mm) and relatively wide along the DV direction (~1.8mm) at the coronal plane of microinjection. (b) Schematic illustration (left) and representative result (right) of MRI-informed coronal angled stereotactic microinjection into intrapontine trigeminal roots of adult SD rats. Considering the angle scale values of the coronal tilt, the coronal 18<sup>&#x000b0;</sup> angled stereotactic microinjection from the midline was finally found to robustly target intrapontine trigeminal roots at the stereotactic coordinates (AP -9.86 mm, ML 2.85 mm, DV -8.77 mm). N = 3 animals.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
</p><p>
<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="MOESM20"><media xlink:href="10194_2025_2162_MOESM20_ESM.pptx"><caption><p>Additional file 20: Movie S1. Representative video of persistent asymmetric eyelid contraction and asymmetric cluster face-stroking evoked by air puffs at 2.50 psi seven days after LPC (A) and PBS (B) microinjection into adult rat trigeminal REZ.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material>
