itutional affiliations.</p></fn><fn><p>Zhi-Yang Wang and You-Quan Ding contributed equally to this work.</p></fn></fn-group><ack><title>Acknowledgements</title><p>We give our thanks to Prof. Xin-Fu Zhou (Sansom Institute, School of Pharmacy and Medical Sciences, University of South Australia) for his help in the organization and language editing of the manuscript.</p></ack><notes notes-type="author-contribution"><title>Authors&#x02019; contributions</title><p>ZYW performed scalable surgical, histological and behavioral experiments in rat and mouse model of trigeminal REZ demyelination. YQD conceived and designed the study, established the experimental workflow for all the experiments, analyzed all the data, prepared the figures and wrote the manuscript. JMW performed scalable surgical, histological and behavioral experiments in rat model of intrapontine trigeminal root demyelination. BWZ performed MRI experiments and analyzed these MRI data. KZ provided theoretical information for rodent brain MRI atlas, designed MRI experiments and analyzed these MRI data. JGQ conceived and designed the study, supervised the execution of this project, and supervised data interpretation and manuscript preparation. All the authors read and approved the final manuscript.</p></notes><notes notes-type="funding-information"><title>Funding</title><p>The work reported herein was supported by grants from National Natural Science Foundation of China (31571240) to Jian-Guo Qi and Sichuan Provincial Key Laboratory of Development and Regeneration to You-Quan Ding (SYS19-01), Zhi-Yang Wang (SYS20-03) and Ju-Mei Wen (SYS22-01).</p></notes><notes notes-type="data-availability"><title>Data availability</title><p>No datasets were generated or analysed during the current study.</p></notes><notes><title>Declarations</title><notes id="FPar1"><title>Ethics approval and consent to participate</title><p id="Par109">All the animal manipulations were performed with the approval of the Animal Care and Ethics Committee of Sichuan University (approval number: SCU44-2503-04) and in strict accordance with the National Institutes of Health Guide for the Care and Use of Laboratory Animals (publication no. 85&#x02013;23, revised 1985).</p></notes><notes id="FPar2"><title>Consent for publication</title><p id="Par110">Not applicable.</p></notes><notes id="FPar3" notes-type="COI-statement"><title>Competing interests</title><p id="Par111">The authors declare no competing interests.</p></notes></notes><ref-list id="Bib1"><title>References</title><ref id="CR1"><label>1.</label><citation-alternatives><element-citation id="ec-CR1" publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ashina</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Robertson</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Srikiatkhachorn</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Di Stefano</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Donnet</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hodaie</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Obermann</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Romero-Reyes</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>YS</given-names></name><name><surname>Cruccu</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bendtsen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trigeminal neuralgia</article-title><source>Nat Rev Dis Primers</source><year>2024</year><volume>10</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>39</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/s41572-024-00523-z</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">38816415</pub-id>
